msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:44
#: 3fd1ea60ff3644d49e4c7a0c4361559a
msgid "How to invoke AutoTune"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:46
#: c7d1bc1725c94984a25f260344b940a6
msgid "Wait for a calm day and go to a large open area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:47
#: 17e49cd6b542442295b47e1978d7e416
msgid "Ensure the Aux AUTOTUNE switch, if used, is in the LOW position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:48
#: ba27f49ff5cd4033b258c4640f290ff0
msgid "Take off and put the copter into AltHold mode at a comfortable altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:50
#: 713f00ed1dc547b9a8642fcb11d8c458
msgid "Face the vehicle so that it will twitch at 90degrees from the direction the wind is blowing (i.e. if tuning Roll first, point the vehicle into the wind)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:55
#: ae4c1035b62643d68f255caccefe4e8a
msgid "Set the AUX switch to the HIGH position, or switch to AUTOTUNE mode, to engage auto tuning:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:57
#: 15479f8da8df4fbab4f33881b5850d42
msgid "You will see it twitch about 20 degrees left and right for a few minutes, then it will repeat forward and back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:59
#: 0c8c3fcf54c041dd96e5ed012d66f361
msgid "Use the roll and pitch stick at any time to reposition the copter if it drifts away (it will use the original PID gains during repositioning and between tests).  When you release the sticks it will continue auto tuning where it left off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:63
#: 16c061bd6a1d49b7bec4687bca601e45
msgid "Move the AUX switch into the LOW position, or change flight mode if using AUTOTUNE flight mode, at any time to abandon the autotuning and return to the origin PIDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:65
#: 7ab30709d416490880d8e2cb0d486f57
msgid "Make sure that you do not have any trim set on your transmitter or the autotune may not get the signal that the sticks are centered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:68
#: 5aaf6e68191e45b6b99d461aca93fc07
msgid "When the tune completes the copter will change back to the original PID gains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:70
#: f2a753bdd4f1499e8192615f667c2c2b
msgid "Put the AUX switch into the LOW position and then back to the HIGH position to test the tuned PID gains, or if using the AUTOTUNE flight mode, switch out and then back into that mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:72
#: e47d785923214310b53c3bbec60d0d3a
msgid "Put the AUXswitch into the LOW position, or switch out of AUTOTUNE flight mode, to fly using the original PID gains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:73
#: dd66baeba843458e980edc3b79fd1875
msgid "If you are happy with the autotuned PID gains, leave the AUX switch in the HIGH position, or switch back into AUTOTUNE flight mode and land and disarm to save the PIDs permanently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:76
#: 90f1957d165d41a5b88bd7627f406357
msgid "If you DO NOT like the new PIDS, switch the AUX switch LOW or out of AUTOTUNE flight mode, to return to the original PIDs. The gains will not be saved when you disarm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:78
#: 09bbacbd2fdb4c85b6ae5710d24d22da
msgid "If you find after performing an AutoTune that the vehicle feels overly twitchy when flying Stabilize, AltHold or PosHold (but ok in more autonomous modes like Loiter, RTL, Auto) try increasing the :ref:`ATC_INPUT_TC<ATC_INPUT_TC>` parameter to 0.25.  This smooths out the pilot's input. Alternatively try reducing the :ref:`AUTOTUNE_AGGR <AUTOTUNE_AGGR>` parameter (it should always be in the range 0.05 to 0.10) and try again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:82
#: f9ede0a889744d3cbe17f91ec3702601
msgid "If the vehicle feels sloppy after the AutoTune, try increasing the :ref:`AUTOTUNE_AGGR <AUTOTUNE_AGGR>` parameter as high as 0.10 and attempt the autotune again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:85
#: 046fecf32a424265aaa622ad577da8a2
msgid "Invoke AutoTune with Position Hold"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:89
#: 29988ad8d2f14ac8b4fdf5fdf76e4ce9
msgid "A better tune can often be achieved by invoking AutoTune from AltHold as described above instead of from Loiter or PosHold as described below. Using AUTOTUNE flight mode also has this possible disadvantage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:91
#: 9a5358a8beea4440953750f9f5435d33
msgid "AutoTune performs a weak position hold if invoked from Loiter or PosHold flight modes (as opposed to AltHold) while doing an autotune. If using the AUTOTUNE flight mode, this weak position hold is also used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:97
#: c92f4fe7bd31485ea2ed29a9a1e6dbeb
msgid "The vehicle will gently lean (up to 10 degrees) towards a \"target point\" which is initially set to the vehicle's location at the moment AutoTune was invoked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:98
#: 6c3f7dd240f044ce97486c50de756daa
msgid "The pilot can reposition the vehicle using the roll, pitch, yaw or throttle sticks.  The target position will be reset to the vehicle's location at the moment the pilot releases the roll and pitch sticks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:99
#: 90a77ba0696540f49b326f38056e703f
msgid "The altitude is maintained with the altitude hold controller so the vehicle will attempt to hold its current altitude when the sticks are placed with 10% of mid-throttle. It will climb or descend at up to 2.5m/s (this speed is adjustable with the :ref:`PILOT_SPD_UP<PILOT_SPD_UP>` and :ref:`PILOT_SPD_DN<PILOT_SPD_DN>` parameters). The acceleration used to establish these speeds is set by :ref:`PILOT_ACC_Z<PILOT_ACC_Z>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:104
#: 29716c9c0e324bb087a4e6ce2c7b4ce5
msgid "To twitch perpendicular to the wind direction, the vehicle may suddenly rotate in either direction up to 90 degrees as it drifts 5m (or more) from the target location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:105
#: 80dbb80ece5144c28477ae0842327dcb
msgid "If there is little or no wind, the vehicle's gentle position control may mean it moves back and forth, ping-ponging around the target point changing yaw each time it strays more than 5m from the target.  In these cases, it may be more comfortable to revert to the simpler AltHold-based AutoTune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:108
#: 9ccb3a78fef840be952a2e9143e246c8
msgid "Testing Tune in Other Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:110
#: 898351e2c940497da3641687dfec2b3d
msgid "The completed suceesfull tune obtained can be tested in any mode, not just the one (ALTHOLD or LOITER) used for entry. A switch can be setup,``RCx_OPTION`` = 180 (AUTOTUNE_TEST_GAINS) that will allow switching between original and autotuned gains in any mode, after autotune has completed. If this switch is setup, but not changed after the auotune has completed, it has no effect. Otherwise if switched high the tuned gains are in effect, if low the original gains. Then they apply to any flight mode and will be made permanent upon the next disarm, based on  switch position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:113
#: 6f0277bfc4fc4ddaa0d4538592930238
msgid "If AutoTune fails"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotune.rst:115
#: bb603dfa04574d0dbb5c3d41345560e1
